  "page1": {
    "title": "The Magnet You Can Switch On",
    "subtitle": "How electricity can turn a plain iron nail into a magnet you control.",
    "body": "A normal magnet is always on. But an electromagnet can turn on and off, like a switch.\n\nInside it, a long wire is wrapped around an iron nail. When electric current flows through the wire, the nail becomes a magnet. This power that pulls iron is called magnetic force.\n\nThe current makes this force around the iron core. So the nail can pull clips and pins. When you stop the current, the magnet turns off. Then the clips fall, because the force is gone.\n\nYou can also make it stronger. If you wrap more wire, the force grows. A bigger battery gives more power.\n\nPeople use electromagnets in machines. Big cranes <mark>lift heavy metal</mark> with them. They can grab the metal and drop it when they want.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/venus/2026-07/01.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "A wire wrapped around an iron nail becomes a magnet when current flows, and a crane lifting metal.",
